 "notes": "Libretto by Lorenzo Da Ponte (1790). Words follow the Peters engraving's spelling and punctuation: macchine (the libretto has machine), vorebbe, quà, Si and di si without accents, com' io and Or ben as two words. Despina's Me lo dona? (the libretto has Me la dona?) and è loro il mio giulebbe (the libretto has È l'oro) are kept as printed; loro is glossed and pronounced as l'oro, the gold Don Alfonso has just shown her. Despina's aside “Per me questa mi preme” is not set in this score. Don Alfonso's avrai and sai and Despina's lei and proposizione are sung in more syllables than they are spelt, and their IPA follows the score. IPA, word meanings and translations come from the app's reviewed Così libretto drafts (L26, IPA checked against Castel). IPA follows sung Italian conventions: stressed syllable marked, elisions (two words on one note in the score) joined with ‿, open e/o as ɛ/ɔ. Translation literal, for meaning.",
